    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster presents a high-upside outlook for today\u2019s slate, anchored by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers as our only elite play (81.88). Facing Jack Flaherty, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an immense +16% park factor and a robust +14% dynamic platoon edge, positioning him as the primary offensive engine. Following him, we see a tier of strong contributors led by **Josh Jung** (61.62), who enjoys a favorable matchup against Grayson Rodriguez\u2019s high 5.91 xERA. **Dominic Smith** (60.26) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (59.93) are also prioritized in the daily optimization; **Dominic Smith** capitalizes on a weak pitching matchup against Miles Mikolas (+17% SP Skill), while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a consistent staple in our order, even when battling the slight hurdle of a dynamic platoon disadvantage.\n\nManaging the volatility of \"Lineup Pending\" statuses requires careful navigation, particularly in the outfield. **Sam Antonacci** (48.07) earns a spot largely due to his lead-off position (+10% order bonus) and a favorable wind-out forecast (+5%), though he faces a challenging outing against Trevor McDonald. The bench decision for **Andy Pages** (44.57) was the most difficult; he narrowly missed the cut behind **Coby Mayo** (48.97), as the optimizer prioritized **Coby Mayo**'s park-adjusted ceiling over **Andy Pages**'s slightly more neutral expectation. Owners should remain wary of the heavy hitters facing elite arms today; **Josh Lowe** and **Kyle Tucker** are both starting despite significant 19% SP skill penalties associated with opposing aces Jacob deGrom and Logan Henderson. While these stars are capable of producing, their efficiency scores reflect the heightened risk of facing such elite talent. Finally, with **Jordan Westburg** confirmed on the IL, we will continue to lean on **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (59.52) to anchor the middle infield alongside **Nasim Nunez**, provided they confirm in their expected roles.",
